Operations and Human Resources Manager Mid senior Onsite Operations Management, Human Resources Management, Supply Chain Management, Logistics, Distribution, Warehouse Operations, Equipment Maintenance, Inventory Management, Recruitment, Conflict Resolution, Employee Relations, Training and Development, HR Policy and Compliance, Leadership, Team Management, Communication, Interpersonal Skills, Confidentiality, Performance Management, Retail, Food Service, Packaging, French (oral and written), English (functional), Bachelor's degree in Operations Management Human Resources Business Administration or related field, 3 to 5 years of relevant experience in operations and human resources management, Strong understanding of supply chain logistics and distribution processes, Strong leadership and team management skills, Exceptional interpersonal and communication abilities, Demonstrated ability to meet and exceed performance targets and deadlines Operations Management, Human Resources Management, Supply Chain Management, Logistics, Distribution, Warehouse Operations, Equipment Maintenance, Inventory Management, Recruitment, Conflict Resolution, Employee Relations, Training and Development, HR Policy and Compliance, Leadership, Team Management, Communication, Interpersonal Skills, Confidentiality, Performance Management, Retail, Food Service, Packaging, French (oral and written), English (functional), Bachelors degree in Operations Management Human Resources Business Administration or related field, 3 to 5 years of relevant experience in operations and human resources management, Strong understanding of supply chain logistics and distribution processes, Strong leadership and team management skills, Exceptional interpersonal and communication abilities, Demonstrated ability to meet and exceed performance targets and deadlines LOOKING FOR AN
OPERATIONS AND HUMAN RESOURCES MANAGER
Are you interested in joining a friendly team, in a position with stimulating challenges? If so, this opportunity is for you!
About The Opportunity
Workland presents a unique career opportunity within a family-owned and leading Canadian distributor of retail, food service, and packaging products, located in the Saint-Laurent area of Montreal. The company is seeking an experienced, talented, and versatile Operations and Human Resources Manager to join the team. This position offers a unique opportunity to contribute to both the operational efficiency and human capital development of the organization.
WHY SHOULD THIS OPPORTUNITY INTEREST YOU?
Friendly working environment
Inspiring and stimulating work culture
Competitive compensation and benefits package
Work-life balance
Join a company that offers stability and a welcoming atmosphere
A company that thinks about the environment
Opportunity to lead a team of seasoned professionals
Support and training provided to maximize your potential
Opportunities for career advancement and professional development
Opportunity to contribute to the success of diversified business lines (retail, food service, and packaging products)
Job Description
As the Operations and Human Resources Manager, you will play a pivotal role in optimizing the organization’s distribution processes while fostering a positive and productive workplace. This role requires a strategic mindset to enhance operational efficiency and a hands-on approach to address human resources needs. The ideal candidate will possess a strong background in both operations management and human resources.
Your Tasks And Responsibilities Will Be
Oversee and streamline the end-to-end supply chain processes, ensuring timely and efficient delivery of products to clients;
Collaborate with logistics partners, suppliers, and internal teams to optimize inventory levels;
Manage day-to-day operations of distribution facilities, including warehouse operations, equipment maintenance, and safety protocols;
Implement best practices to enhance operational efficiency and minimize costs;
Work closely with department heads to identify staffing needs and develop effective recruitment strategies;
Lead the recruitment process, from candidate sourcing to onboarding;
Foster a positive work environment by addressing employee concerns, resolving conflicts, and promoting open communication;
Conduct investigations and provide guidance, on employee relations matters;
Identify training needs and collaborate with department heads to design and implement effective training programs;
Facilitate workshops and training sessions to enhance employee skills and knowledge;
Develop and update HR policies to ensure compliance with labor laws and company standards;
Stay informed about changes in employment legislation and proactively address compliance issues;
Any other related duties required.
The Requirements For This Position Are
Bachelor's degree in Operations Management, Human Resources, Business Administration, or related field;
3 to 5 years of relevant experience in operations and human resources management, preferably in the distribution industry*;
Strong understanding of supply chain, logistics, and distribution processes;
Strong leadership and team management skills;
Exceptional interpersonal and communication abilities;
Ability to handle sensitive information with confidentiality;
Demonstrated ability to meet and exceed performance targets and deadlines;
In-depth knowledge of the Canadian retail, food service, and packaging product distribution markets, is an asset;
Fluency in French (oral and written) and English (functional).
Any other combination of relevant experience may be considered.
About Workland
Workland is proud to have been mandated in the recruitment process for this job opportunity. Workland's mission is to accelerate and facilitate the connection between the best talent and the right organizations, through an approach that promotes diversity, equity, and inclusion in the workplace.
