Registered Nurse (RN) or Registered Practical Nurse (RPN) or Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) with current registration with the Provincial Licensing Body;
Diploma in Gerontology, Nursing Administration, Rehabilitation, or the equivalent;
Completion or working towards a course in adult education at the community college level is considered an asset;
Must possess good written and oral communication skills;
Good motivational and time management skills, good inter-departmental communications and leadership skills are necessary;
